# 1. Clone the repository
git clone [https://github.com/vyshakhak/vcapture.git](https://github.com/vyshakhak/vcapture.git)
cd vcapture

# 2. Make the script executable
chmod +x vcapture.py

# 3. Move it to your local binaries folder
sudo mv vcapture.py /usr/local/bin/vcapture

💻 Usage
Because vcapture interacts directly with network interface cards, it must be run with sudo.

Basic Usage (Sniff on the default interface indefinitely):

Bash
sudo vcapture
Specify a Network Interface:

Bash
sudo vcapture -i eth0
Limit the Number of Captured Packets:

Bash
sudo vcapture -i wlan0 -c 50
Help Menu:

Bash
vcapture -h
